1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:06,367
I really do like Serizawa after all.

2
00:00:06,467 --> 00:00:09,367
I'll match your pace from now on.

3
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:11,100
Huh? My pace?

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,400
So it's true, Serizawa.

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,267
I heard Serizawa has a crush on someone.

6
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:18,743
Apparently, he's had an
unrequited crush since freshman year.

7
00:00:18,767 --> 00:00:21,400
Wow, he's so devoted.

8
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:32,033
Who exactly is Serizawa's crush?

9
00:00:32,267 --> 00:00:33,467
Let me borrow this.

10
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:42,300
But knowing Serizawa, he'd
definitely have a beautiful romance.

11
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:43,733
I'm sorry!

12
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,500
Matsuno?

13
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:48,367
Suzuki.

14
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:50,967
Ah, sorry.

15
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:52,333
Here, use this to wipe it.

16
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Ah...

17
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,467
Thanks.

18
00:00:57,367 --> 00:01:00,067
You don't have to return it.

19
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:08,267
Suzuki!

20
00:01:14,233 --> 00:01:15,467
Or maybe...

21
00:01:16,433 --> 00:01:17,700
Never mind.

22
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:25,767
Suzuki.

23
00:01:27,033 --> 00:01:28,233
What's wrong?

24
00:01:29,733 --> 00:01:30,567
Yeah.

25
00:01:30,667 --> 00:01:32,000
It's nothing.

26
00:01:32,267 --> 00:01:35,600
Was he trying to make up with you?

27
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:38,000
No.

28
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:40,367
We haven't really had
a proper conversation.

29
00:01:41,633 --> 00:01:46,600
Even though we were best
friends in our freshman year.

30
00:01:48,833 --> 00:01:51,200
But right now, Suzuki's best friend...

31
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:52,533
...is me, right?

32
00:01:52,633 --> 00:01:54,167
Don't you forget that.

33
00:01:54,267 --> 00:01:55,267
You're too close...

34
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:58,100
Besides, back in our freshman year,

35
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,100
I already wanted to be friends with Suzuki.

36
00:02:07,633 --> 00:02:13,667
I wish I had met Serizawa
in my freshman year, too.

37
00:02:15,167 --> 00:02:17,333
By the way, Suzuki.

38
00:02:17,433 --> 00:02:19,500
Want to go to the beach with me?

39
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:20,967
The beach?

40
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:21,567
Yeah.

41
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:23,533
Let's make some summer memories together.

42
00:02:23,633 --> 00:02:25,067
Suzuki.

43
00:03:07,467 --> 00:03:10,467
Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me.

44
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:22,467
(Episode 8)

45
00:03:22,567 --> 00:03:24,367
Summer memories...

46
00:03:26,733 --> 00:03:28,133
Suzuki!

47
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,067
Over here, over here!

48
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:39,733
Just the two of us...

49
00:03:54,633 --> 00:03:56,233
As if that would happen.

50
00:03:57,633 --> 00:03:59,533
Huh? Isn't that Suzuki?

51
00:04:02,633 --> 00:04:04,333
You finally made it.

52
00:04:04,733 --> 00:04:06,333
I'm so glad.

53
00:04:07,233 --> 00:04:08,233
Let's go together.

54
00:04:09,133 --> 00:04:10,400
Yeah.

55
00:04:20,633 --> 00:04:22,353
- That's a pretty good shot.
- It really is.

56
00:04:23,167 --> 00:04:28,467
I didn't know girls were coming, too.

57
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:32,167
These guys are way too outgoing...

58
00:04:33,467 --> 00:04:36,533
Could Serizawa's crush...

59
00:04:36,633 --> 00:04:38,333
...be one of them?

60
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:41,500
Miyamoto-san?

61
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,067
Takahashi-san?

62
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,233
Sakuraba-san?

63
00:04:46,233 --> 00:04:48,633
She's Saeki's girlfriend, so probably not.

64
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:50,567
Suzuki!

65
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,167
Why are you staring at the girls?

66
00:04:55,633 --> 00:04:57,367
I... I'm not.

67
00:04:57,467 --> 00:04:58,533
Come on, let's go.

68
00:05:02,467 --> 00:05:05,067
Aren't you getting in the water?

69
00:05:05,233 --> 00:05:07,367
No, it's just...

70
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:13,433
Everyone's just so energetic.

71
00:05:15,167 --> 00:05:16,233
You're hopeless.

72
00:05:18,533 --> 00:05:21,100
Didn't we agree to make
some summer memories together?

73
00:05:23,667 --> 00:05:25,367
Come on, let's go.

74
00:06:01,433 --> 00:06:02,600
Huh?

75
00:06:03,133 --> 00:06:04,500
Suzuki is out!

76
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,933
Se... Serizawa!

77
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:08,300
If you're frustrated, fight back!

78
00:06:09,733 --> 00:06:11,167
Jeez...

79
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:14,333
So frustrating.

80
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:22,467
Whenever I'm with Serizawa,
I always end up getting dragged along.

81
00:06:36,733 --> 00:06:43,000
I really do... like Serizawa.

82
00:06:44,067 --> 00:06:45,233
Bring it on, bring it on!

83
00:06:45,333 --> 00:06:49,733
Serizawa... wait up...

84
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,333
Reon.

85
00:07:05,433 --> 00:07:06,467
Huh?

86
00:07:06,733 --> 00:07:08,167
- Let me have a sip.
- Huh?

87
00:07:09,633 --> 00:07:11,367
Hey, wait, you're drinking too much!

88
00:07:11,467 --> 00:07:14,167
- What's the big deal?
- Hey, why? Give it back!

89
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,467
Could it be...

90
00:07:19,133 --> 00:07:20,333
More, more!

91
00:07:23,167 --> 00:07:24,967
Stop moving around!

92
00:07:25,067 --> 00:07:27,200
- Hurry up.
- Yeah...

93
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:29,109
- What's wrong? Got sand in your eye?
- Don't splash it in my face!

94
00:07:29,133 --> 00:07:31,133
Did you do that on purpose?

95
00:07:34,267 --> 00:07:38,600
Serizawa's crush is...

96
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,200
Here you go.

97
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,067
Huh? Are you sure?

98
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:49,467
Ah, actually, that'll be 10,000 yen.

99
00:07:49,567 --> 00:07:50,733
That's way too expensive!

100
00:07:52,367 --> 00:07:53,367
Thanks.

101
00:07:53,433 --> 00:07:54,600
Yeah.

102
00:07:59,767 --> 00:08:01,233
Having fun?

103
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,333
Yeah.

104
00:08:05,633 --> 00:08:10,433
But... is it really okay for me to be here?

105
00:08:11,233 --> 00:08:12,967
Of course it is.

106
00:08:13,067 --> 00:08:17,600
Besides, everyone likes
you more than you think.

107
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,267
Thanks.

108
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,733
Takeuchi, you're such a nice guy.

109
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,333
No, it's not like that...

110
00:08:31,333 --> 00:08:32,333
By the way.

111
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:38,500
Have you guys been
close since freshman year?

112
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:41,200
Yeah, we've been pretty tight.

113
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:44,400
I was the only one in a
different class back then.

114
00:08:46,267 --> 00:08:47,467
I see...

115
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,633
I knew it...

116
00:08:52,033 --> 00:08:55,500
Ah! You two are sneaking Ramune!

117
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,400
So lucky.

118
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,400
Get up.

119
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:57,967
Got anything to drink?

120
00:08:58,067 --> 00:08:59,233
Ah, so unfair.

121
00:08:59,333 --> 00:09:00,333
Where's ours?

122
00:09:00,433 --> 00:09:01,500
How should I know?

123
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:02,267
Go buy it yourselves.

124
00:09:02,367 --> 00:09:04,300
- See you later.
- So cold.

125
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,433
Then Serizawa can go buy some.

126
00:09:06,533 --> 00:09:07,533
Why me?

127
00:09:07,567 --> 00:09:10,067
Come on, I'm thirsty, too.

128
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:12,167
Please, Serizawa.

129
00:09:14,067 --> 00:09:15,233
You guys are hopeless.

130
00:09:16,333 --> 00:09:19,333
Ah, Suzuki, let's go buy some together.

131
00:09:24,733 --> 00:09:26,033
Suzuki?

132
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,067
Let's go.

133
00:09:36,167 --> 00:09:37,200
Huh?

134
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:41,500
Serizawa?

135
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,767
Yeah?

136
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:45,500
We're still holding hands...

137
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:48,200
Yeah, I know.

138
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:52,067
Are you mad?

139
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:53,667
Not at all.

140
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:58,067
But why were you staring at Reon earlier?

141
00:09:58,733 --> 00:10:04,567
Because Miyamoto-san and you
seemed so close...

142
00:10:05,733 --> 00:10:07,100
What do you mean?

143
00:10:11,433 --> 00:10:15,300
Suzuki, are you jealous?

144
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:16,533
No.

145
00:10:16,633 --> 00:10:20,233
It's not that... It's just that recently,

146
00:10:22,067 --> 00:10:24,167
I overheard some seniors talking.

147
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:31,967
They said you have a crush on someone...

148
00:10:32,067 --> 00:10:33,200
Huh?

149
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:39,067
So I was wondering if it was Miyamoto-san.

150
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:41,333
Definitely not.

151
00:10:42,467 --> 00:10:44,600
Then... Takahashi-san?

152
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:46,033
No.

153
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,567
Could it be Sakuraba-san?

154
00:10:48,667 --> 00:10:49,900
No way.

155
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,600
She's Saeki's girlfriend.

156
00:10:53,067 --> 00:10:54,200
True...

157
00:10:56,333 --> 00:11:00,700
But I do have a crush on someone.

158
00:11:04,333 --> 00:11:05,533
Haven't you noticed?

159
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,633
Even though they're always right beside me.

160
00:11:09,733 --> 00:11:11,167
Huh?

161
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:14,300
They're really great.

162
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:18,733
Cute, gentle, and hardworking.

163
00:11:22,533 --> 00:11:25,600
But incredibly dense.

164
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:29,167
We were in the same class for
the first time in our sophomore year.

165
00:11:29,267 --> 00:11:31,233
Even though I've dropped so many hints,

166
00:11:31,256 --> 00:11:33,690
they hasn't noticed my feelings at all.

167
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:42,967
But I even find that
part really cute.

168
00:11:43,067 --> 00:11:44,333
That's why I love them.

169
00:11:51,467 --> 00:11:52,733
So?

170
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:56,667
Any idea who it is?

171
00:12:09,633 --> 00:12:10,633
Want some more?

172
00:12:11,067 --> 00:12:12,143
- You guys better finish it all.
- We will.

173
00:12:12,167 --> 00:12:13,327
- Really?
- Add a little more.

174
00:12:13,367 --> 00:12:14,033
Want more?

175
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:15,553
Nice, that'll get the fire going.

176
00:12:15,633 --> 00:12:18,073
- Are you sure?
- I forgot you've never grilled meat yourself.

177
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:20,600
- No way.
- Stop teasing her.

178
00:12:22,667 --> 00:12:25,467
I have absolutely no idea...

179
00:12:26,433 --> 00:12:28,967
Or rather, my heart was beating so fast,

180
00:12:29,067 --> 00:12:31,700
I barely heard a word he said.

181
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:34,700
Why hasn't he noticed at all?

182
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:39,333
He's way too dense.

183
00:12:39,433 --> 00:12:42,067
I've dropped so many hints.

184
00:12:42,167 --> 00:12:45,633
Well, it is Suzuki we're talking about.

185
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:48,167
He'd never get it just from hints.

186
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:49,633
Come on, at this point,

187
00:12:49,733 --> 00:12:51,400
why not just tell him directly?

188
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,667
Like this:

189
00:12:53,233 --> 00:12:55,200
I like you, Suzuki!

190
00:12:55,633 --> 00:12:57,667
- Huh?
- Don't make it sound so easy.

191
00:12:57,767 --> 00:13:01,633
I've been closing the distance
little by little since our freshman year.

192
00:13:01,733 --> 00:13:03,667
It took a lot to get to where we are today.

193
00:13:05,033 --> 00:13:08,100
I'm definitely not
letting Suzuki slip away.

194
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,576
Serizawa, you're being a little scary.

195
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:14,600
But I get how you feel.

196
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:18,567
You don't want to confess and end up
causing him trouble or making him worry.

197
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,500
Yeah...

198
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:23,600
If only Suzuki's heart could lean...

199
00:13:24,767 --> 00:13:26,433
...just a little bit toward me.

200
00:13:27,767 --> 00:13:31,367
I wonder... what he really thinks of me.

201
00:13:33,467 --> 00:13:34,567
Wait.

202
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:35,533
No way.

203
00:13:35,633 --> 00:13:37,067
Really?

204
00:13:37,167 --> 00:13:39,533
- I put it in.
- The person Serizawa likes...

205
00:13:39,633 --> 00:13:41,967
Who could it be?

206
00:13:42,067 --> 00:13:43,333
Suzuki.

207
00:13:44,033 --> 00:13:45,100
Thank you.

208
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,100
Oh, it's nothing.

209
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:49,267
I don't mind cooking anyway.

210
00:13:50,367 --> 00:13:52,667
Not just that. I want to
thank you for coming today.

211
00:13:52,767 --> 00:13:53,500
Huh?

212
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:57,333
By the way, how did you
and Serizawa get so close?

213
00:13:58,333 --> 00:14:01,433
I asked before, but I
didn't get a clear answer.

214
00:14:01,533 --> 00:14:04,500
I was wondering what sparked it.

215
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:09,667
It started because...

216
00:14:10,733 --> 00:14:13,667
I like BL and stuff.

217
00:14:13,767 --> 00:14:15,067
BL?

218
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,300
Yeah.

219
00:14:18,067 --> 00:14:19,367
Ah, I see.

220
00:14:19,467 --> 00:14:21,600
Serizawa really does like BL, after all.

221
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:23,633
You knew?

222
00:14:23,733 --> 00:14:26,133
He used to read it a
lot in our freshman year.

223
00:14:26,233 --> 00:14:29,200
I've read some too.
It's actually pretty good.

224
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:30,400
Yeah.

225
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:33,900
Oh, speaking of which,
it was really sudden back then.

226
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,509
Serizawa suddenly got obsessed with BL.

227
00:14:35,533 --> 00:14:36,233
Huh?

228
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,200
Ah, right.

229
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,067
During his freshman year.

230
00:14:40,167 --> 00:14:43,233
He said he started reading it
because of someone he liked.

231
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:47,167
Someone he liked...

232
00:14:48,233 --> 00:14:49,433
Huh?

233
00:14:49,567 --> 00:14:52,333
Wait a minute, could it be...

234
00:14:53,733 --> 00:14:55,500
Is it possible...

235
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,333
That's what's going on?

236
00:15:00,467 --> 00:15:01,467
Oh, stop it.

237
00:15:05,967 --> 00:15:07,600
What do you mean?

238
00:15:10,333 --> 00:15:11,433
Mmm!

239
00:15:12,033 --> 00:15:13,043
It tastes like protein powder.

240
00:15:13,067 --> 00:15:13,633
- What protein?
- Hey, that's not right.

241
00:15:13,733 --> 00:15:14,733
- Look, look!
- Uh...

242
00:15:14,767 --> 00:15:17,133
- Don't be a third wheel here.
- Hey!

243
00:15:18,067 --> 00:15:19,627
- I feel like he was getting in the way.
- Yeah.

244
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:21,300
Okay, take a bite.

245
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,600
I'm pouring it.

246
00:15:24,053 --> 00:15:25,219
- Okay.
- Here.

247
00:15:25,667 --> 00:15:26,667
That's spicy.

248
00:15:29,067 --> 00:15:32,200
So, the person Serizawa likes...

249
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:35,533
He's had an unrequited crush
on them since freshman year.

250
00:15:35,633 --> 00:15:38,600
They already knew each other back then.

251
00:15:40,067 --> 00:15:44,100
But they weren't in the same
class until sophomore year.

252
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,100
Didn't you notice?

253
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,100
They've been right
beside me this whole time.

254
00:15:49,267 --> 00:15:53,400
Someone who's always
around and also likes BL...

255
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:54,900
Is that what it means?

256
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:58,767
But... who fits all those descriptions?

257
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,467
Suzuki, are you eating any meat?

258
00:16:02,067 --> 00:16:03,067
Here.

259
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,667
- Thanks.
- Wait a minute!

260
00:16:07,267 --> 00:16:08,267
Wait, what?

261
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:11,500
Here, Suzuki, eat the one I grilled.

262
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:12,333
Huh?

263
00:16:12,433 --> 00:16:14,167
It's the same no matter who grills it.

264
00:16:14,267 --> 00:16:15,367
No, it's not.

265
00:16:15,567 --> 00:16:17,767
This meat is made with love.

266
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,033
Love?

267
00:16:19,133 --> 00:16:20,000
Love.

268
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:21,400
- What, what?
- Here.

269
00:16:22,767 --> 00:16:24,133
Thanks.

270
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:28,067
What's all this about love?

271
00:16:34,333 --> 00:16:35,600
By the way...

272
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:39,267
I'd love to read the
novel you wrote, Suzuki.

273
00:16:39,633 --> 00:16:41,200
I like BL too.

274
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,640
You like it too, Takeuchi?

275
00:16:42,667 --> 00:16:45,400
I've been reading it
even longer than Serizawa.

276
00:16:46,067 --> 00:16:48,733
In freshman year, I was the
only one in a different class.

277
00:16:50,367 --> 00:16:51,533
Could it be...

278
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:53,633
Suzuki?

279
00:16:53,733 --> 00:16:55,067
Aren't you going to eat?

280
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:57,633
Ah, no...

281
00:16:59,467 --> 00:17:03,300
Takeuchi, you and Serizawa went
to the same middle school, right?

282
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,300
Yeah, we did.

283
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:08,567
Were you in the same class?

284
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:11,700
No.

285
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:15,767
We weren't in the same
class until sophomore year.

286
00:17:17,433 --> 00:17:23,300
But we got close during our freshman year.

287
00:17:23,767 --> 00:17:26,300
We were both on the library committee.

288
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:30,567
What's wrong?

289
00:17:32,067 --> 00:17:33,267
Nothing...

290
00:17:36,267 --> 00:17:38,033
Oh crap! The marshmallow is on fire!

291
00:17:38,133 --> 00:17:39,200
Takeuchi, come quick!

292
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:40,333
Hurry!

293
00:17:41,233 --> 00:17:43,100
What on earth are you doing?

294
00:17:44,767 --> 00:17:47,067
Wow, it's burning...

295
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:49,067
Hot, hot!

296
00:17:49,467 --> 00:17:50,767
Are you kidding me?

297
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:53,453
- No way, you're not messing with me, right?
- I found him.

298
00:17:54,333 --> 00:17:57,033
The person who fits every description.

299
00:17:58,767 --> 00:18:00,100
- Wow, so pretty.
- Here we go.

300
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:00,667
That's awesome.

301
00:18:00,767 --> 00:18:02,600
Here it comes, here it comes...

302
00:18:14,033 --> 00:18:15,033
- So cute.
- Right?

303
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:16,100
Give me one too.

304
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,300
Be careful.

305
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:27,100
Youth is in full swing.

306
00:18:44,067 --> 00:18:45,200
So that's how it is.

307
00:18:45,533 --> 00:18:46,733
It's Takeuchi.

308
00:18:47,333 --> 00:18:51,900
Takeuchi is really gentle
and has a mind of his own.

309
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,733
He's a great guy.

310
00:18:55,333 --> 00:18:56,533
It's just...

311
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:01,567
- Serizawa, give me a light.
- Here...

312
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:22,467
Serizawa...

313
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,467
What should I do?

314
00:19:27,233 --> 00:19:32,400
I don't know why... my chest hurts so much.

315
00:19:35,033 --> 00:19:36,533
Yours is way too bright.

316
00:19:36,633 --> 00:19:38,533
- How is it bright?
- It really is!

317
00:19:38,633 --> 00:19:41,300
- Then just surrender peacefully.
- Stop messing around.

318
00:19:52,467 --> 00:19:53,733
Suzuki.

319
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,433
What's up?

320
00:19:56,667 --> 00:19:58,167
Let's light some sparklers together.

321
00:20:00,267 --> 00:20:01,267
Okay.

322
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:06,633
Alright, let's go with this one.

323
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,967
Sparklers?

324
00:20:09,067 --> 00:20:10,067
Yeah.

325
00:20:10,167 --> 00:20:12,200
It really feels like summer, doesn't it?

326
00:20:15,567 --> 00:20:17,333
By the way, did you know?

327
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:24,433
They say if the sparkler's flame lasts until
the very end, your wish will come true.

328
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:26,400
A wish?

329
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:27,567
Yeah.

330
00:20:28,067 --> 00:20:31,200
Right, my wish is this...

331
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:36,533
I hope the person I like will like me back.

332
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:54,033
Wait a minute.

333
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,667
This meat is made with love.

334
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,200
Love?

335
00:20:58,233 --> 00:20:59,467
Love.

336
00:21:06,733 --> 00:21:08,033
What a shame.

337
00:21:10,033 --> 00:21:11,733
Alright, your turn next, Suzuki.

338
00:21:16,067 --> 00:21:19,619
Aren't you going to
make one, Suzuki? A wish.

339
00:21:22,133 --> 00:21:23,300
Yeah.

340
00:21:24,267 --> 00:21:26,167
I'll pass.

341
00:21:26,467 --> 00:21:27,567
Okay.

342
00:21:39,133 --> 00:21:40,967
We're going to a hangout together.

343
00:21:41,066 --> 00:21:42,499
Do you want to come too?

344
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:48,106
Even if you lose your confidence, you're
still challenging yourself now, aren't you?

345
00:21:48,633 --> 00:21:50,200
Isn't that amazing?

346
00:21:50,567 --> 00:21:52,933
Next time, at least say a
proper goodbye to me.

347
00:21:53,033 --> 00:21:55,367
I absolutely love BL too.

348
00:21:55,467 --> 00:21:57,000
What's wrong with that?

349
00:21:58,067 --> 00:22:00,367
Didn't I tell you?

350
00:22:00,467 --> 00:22:02,033
They wouldn't care.

351
00:22:02,133 --> 00:22:03,467
Thank you, Serizawa.

352
00:22:03,733 --> 00:22:07,400
My feelings of thinking
you're great, Suzuki...

353
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:09,033
Just accept them gracefully.

354
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:12,567
Suzuki is cute.

355
00:22:12,667 --> 00:22:16,167
Out of everyone I want by
my side, you're number one.

356
00:22:20,333 --> 00:22:24,467
I really do like Serizawa after all.

357
00:22:27,033 --> 00:22:28,733
Don't you have one, Suzuki?

358
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:31,367
Someone you like.

359
00:22:33,267 --> 00:22:35,567
So, I...

360
00:22:39,700 --> 00:22:41,067
Yeah.

361
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:43,067
No.

362
00:22:49,167 --> 00:22:50,400
I see...

363
00:22:54,067 --> 00:22:59,100
I'm going to root for Serizawa's romance.

364
00:23:00,033 --> 00:23:02,000
(Next Episode Preview)

365
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:03,933
I've been feeling really lonely lately.

366
00:23:04,033 --> 00:23:06,113
And I've been wanting to
hold you like this, Suzuki.

367
00:23:06,567 --> 00:23:10,700
If we keep staying together
like this, I'll definitely...

368
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:13,676
(This drama is purely fictional.)

369
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:14,700
What should I do?
